# Lumenhold Academy — 简体中文 (zh-CN) translation of content/events/pools/courses_b.grim
# Maintained by `node tools/grim.js i18n zh-CN`. Translate the text after "="; keep {tokens}.
# "# en:" shows the English source. [hash] marks the English version a line was translated from;
# lines marked STALE need updating — after fixing the text, delete the [hash] and re-run the tool.


@event illu_candle_drill
# en: The Candle Drill
title [81a84c] = 蜡烛操练
# en: {Illusion I opens with a row of cold candles. Make them burn, Professor Vey says, without burning.|Vey's drawer of candles is open. Every one is older than you.|The candle drill. Some mornings you could do it asleep.} {Vey passes her hand through each flame and says "cold" in the same flat voice.|Someone's flame leans in a draught only it can feel.|The student beside you has made a lovely candle and forgotten the flame.}
text [a2d324] = {幻术 I 以一排冷蜡烛开场。让它们燃烧，维伊教授说，但不许真的烧起来。|维伊那一抽屉蜡烛开着，每一根都比你年纪大。|蜡烛操练。有些早晨你闭着眼都能做。} {维伊把手掌从每一朵火焰中穿过，用同样平板的声音说：“冷的。”|有人的火焰朝一侧倾斜，像在躲一阵只有它感觉得到的穿堂风。|你旁边的同学造出了一根漂亮的蜡烛，却忘了火焰。}
# en: A row of unlit candles on a lecture bench, each crowned with a flame that casts no shadow, a professor holding her palm over one.
scene [f627aa] = 讲台长桌上一排未点燃的蜡烛，每根都顶着一朵不投影子的火焰，一位教授把手掌悬在其中一朵上方。
# en: Hold the flame until it's right
opt.left.label [6ee431] = 守着火焰直到对为止
# en: {Your flame steadies, then flickers in time with your breathing, which Vey says is the point.|Vey's palm hovers over your flame a moment longer than the others. "Almost warm," she says. From her, that's a sonnet.|By the bell your flame has a proper blue heart. You feel oddly proud of something that isn't there.}
opt.left.say.1 [11c5cf] = {你的火焰稳住了，随后跟着你的呼吸一起闪烁，维伊说这正是要点。|维伊的手掌在你的火焰上方比别人多停了一会儿。“几乎是暖的。”她说。出自她口，这简直是一首十四行诗。|下课铃响时，你的火焰有了一颗蓝色的芯。你为一样根本不存在的东西感到莫名骄傲。}
# en: Make it gutter and smoke
opt.right.label [5f6b6b] = 让它摇曳冒烟
# en: {You add a thread of smoke and a little gutter. The student behind you reaches to pinch it out.|Your candle drips wax that isn't there onto a desk that is. Vey watches it fall and says nothing, which means yes.|Your candle gutters and smokes so well that the student beside you lends it their flame. Vey writes "two for one".}
opt.right.say.1 [e4aead] = {你添上一缕烟和一点摇曳。后排的同学伸手想把它掐灭。|你的蜡烛把不存在的蜡滴在真实的桌面上。维伊看着它落下，一言不发，意思是行。|你的蜡烛摇曳冒烟得太逼真，旁边的同学把自己的火苗借给了它。维伊写下“一举两得”。}
# en: {The smoke goes up and the flame goes out, as though embarrassed by its own ambition.|Vey waves a hand through the whole performance. "A candle doesn't try this hard," she says.|You add so much smoke the drill becomes a fog. Vey opens a window that isn't there, and the fog obligingly leaves.}
opt.right.say.2 [b6c491] = {烟升了起来，火却灭了，像是为自己的野心难为情。|维伊一挥手穿过你的整场表演。“蜡烛不会这么卖力。”她说。|你添的烟太多，练习成了一场雾。维伊打开一扇并不存在的窗，雾也很配合地出去了。}

@event illu_one_small_change
# en: One Small Change
title [d7183c] = 一处小改动
# en: {Hand mirrors all round. Glamour your own face, Vey says; change one small thing and hold it.|Out come the mirrors. A glamour you can't hold on yourself, Vey says, won't hold on anyone.|Mirror practice. You know your own face too well by now.} {Vey says people always change their eyes first.|A second-year from Rootward is giving himself a better chin, slowly.|The mirrors fog, as they do {season == "winter": in the cold|when the room warms}.}
text [2e07ab] = {人手一面小镜子。给自己的脸施魅影，维伊说；改一处小地方，并且维持住。|镜子拿出来了。维伊说，连自己身上都撑不住的魅影，在谁身上也撑不住。|镜子练习。到如今你对自己的脸太熟悉了。} {维伊说，人们总是先改眼睛。|一个根庐的二年级生正在慢慢给自己换个更好看的下巴。|镜子起了雾，{season == "winter": 天冷时总是这样。|屋里一暖就会这样。}}
# en: Students bent over little hand mirrors, one changing the colour of her own eyes, another squinting at a nose that isn't quite his.
scene [274c55] = 学生们俯身对着小手镜，一个正在改变自己眼睛的颜色，另一个眯眼看着一只不太像自己的鼻子。
# en: Change something trivial
opt.left.label [1bc550] = 改点无关紧要的
# en: {You move a freckle half an inch. It takes the whole hour. Vey initials your page without looking up.|You darken one eyebrow and keep it dark. Dull, careful work, and the glamour holds.|A small scar vanishes and comes back, vanishes and comes back. By the end it stays gone until you let it.}
opt.left.say.1 [a7b2a4] = {你把一颗雀斑挪了半寸，花了整整一节课。维伊头也不抬地在你的纸上签了字。|你把一边眉毛描深，一直保持着。枯燥又细致的活儿，魅影稳住了。|一道小疤消失又出现，消失又出现。到最后，除非你放手，它一直不见。}
# en: Change what you'd really change
opt.right.label [e542b4] = 改你真正想改的
# en: {It holds beautifully. You look at it longer than the exercise requires, and let it go more slowly than you'd like.|Vey glances over your shoulder. "Ah," she says, kindly enough. "That one. Everybody has one."|You hold it all hour. Afterwards your real face seems slightly unfamiliar, like a coat you've lent out.}
opt.right.say.1 [bf826e] = {它维持得很美。你看它的时间比练习要求的长，放手时也比你愿意的慢。|维伊从你肩后瞥了一眼。“啊，”她说，语气还算温和，“那一处。每个人都有一处。”|你维持了整节课。之后你真正的脸显得有点陌生，像一件借出去又还回来的外套。}

@event illu_spot_the_coin
# en: Spot the Coin
title [5eda6f] = 找出那枚硬币
# en: {Partner work. {partner} lays out three crowns, and one of them is an illusion. Say which.|Three crowns from {partner}. One isn't there, and {they} look{s} pleased about it.|You and {partner} have started keeping score.} {Vey walks the room flicking real coins, to confuse everyone.|The windows are bright and the illusions show it.|The next bench is arguing whether a coin can be "partly fake".}
text [6cbe59] = {搭档练习。{partner}摆出三枚克朗，其中一枚是幻象。说出是哪一枚。|{partner}摆出三枚克朗。有一枚并不存在，{they}看起来对此很得意。|你和{partner}已经开始记分了。} {维伊在教室里走动，往空中弹真硬币，存心把大家搅糊涂。|窗外很亮，幻象在光里露了馅。|隔壁桌在争论一枚硬币能不能“部分是假的”。}
# en: Two students at a bench with three coins between them, one coin shimmering very slightly at the edge.
scene [056f6c] = 两个学生对坐在长桌旁，中间放着三枚硬币，其中一枚边缘微微闪烁。
# en: Study the coins honestly
opt.left.label [1297d9] = 老老实实看硬币
# en: {It's the one with no tarnish. Illusions always come out cleaner than money does.|You stare until your eyes water and pick the middle one. Wrong. {partner} pockets the real two, laughing.|You get it on the third try, by the shine that doesn't move when the light does.}
opt.left.say.1 [69ff81] = {是没有锈迹的那枚。幻象总比真钱干净。|你盯到眼睛发酸，选了中间那枚。错了。{partner}笑着把两枚真的收进口袋。|第三次你猜对了，凭的是那道不随光线移动的反光。}
# en: Watch their face, not the coins
opt.right.label [8b4837] = 看对方的脸，不看硬币
# en: {{partner} glances at the left coin a fraction too fondly. You point. {They} groan{s}.|You keep smiling until {partner} gives it away by smiling back. Vey notes that this isn't the exercise, and that it worked.|You know {partner}'s face by now. {They} know{s} you know, and pick{s} a coin with a straight face to beat you. It doesn't work.}
opt.right.say.1 [fda8ff] = {{partner}瞄向左边那枚的眼神稍稍太温柔了。你一指。{they}哀叹一声。|你一直笑，直到{partner}回了你一个笑，露了底。维伊指出这不是练习的内容，也指出它奏效了。|你现在已经熟悉{partner}的表情了。{they}知道你熟悉，于是板着脸挑了一枚来对付你。没用。}
# en: {{partner} has a better face than you'd thought. Your wrong guess buys {them} a cup of tea.|You watch {partner} so hard you miss the coin blinking out of existence entirely.|{partner} has been practising a blank face in the mirror. It shows. You lose a point and buy the tea.}
opt.right.say.2 [86633f] = {{partner}的表情管理比你想的好。你猜错的代价是请{them}喝一杯茶。|你盯{partner}盯得太用力，完全没看见那枚硬币凭空消失。|{partner}一直在对着镜子练面无表情。看得出来。你丢了一分，还得请喝茶。}

@event illu_bread_smell
# en: The Smell of Bread
title [9ea386] = 面包的香味
# en: {Illusion II adds the other senses. Today, a loaf that looks, smells and sounds fresh when broken.|More bread. Sight is easy, Vey says; smell is where liars are caught.|The bread lesson. The floor smells of loaves that never existed.} {Somebody's loaf smells strongly of wet dog.|One loaf crackles beautifully and smells of nothing.|{gpa >= 3: Vey asks you to go first.|Vey asks you to go last, which feels pointed.}}
text [0bd632] = {幻术 II 加入了其他感官。今天的题目是一条看起来、闻起来、掰开时听起来都新鲜的面包。|面包课还没完。视觉容易，维伊说；骗子都栽在气味上。|面包课。整层楼都弥漫着从未存在过的面包的味道。} {有人的面包浓浓一股湿狗味。|有一条面包咔嚓作响，却什么味道也没有。|{gpa >= 3: 维伊让你第一个来。|维伊让你最后一个来，像是意有所指。}}
# en: A lecture bench with an illusory loaf of bread on a board, steam rising from it, and several students sniffing it doubtfully.
scene [92b758] = 讲台长桌上，木板上放着一条幻象面包，正冒着热气，几个学生半信半疑地凑上去闻。
# en: Get the smell right
opt.left.label [721e15] = 把香味做对
# en: {You spend an hour on the smell of a crust. By the end it's nearly convincing and you're desperately hungry.|You think of a bakery on a cold street and the smell arrives with it. Vey sniffs, and nods once.|The smell is right. The sound of breaking is wrong. Vey says that's the usual order.}
opt.left.say.1 [5c9a39] = {你花了一小时琢磨面包皮的味道。到最后几乎以假乱真，而你饿得发慌。|你想起寒冷街角的一家面包房，香味便随之而来。维伊嗅了嗅，点了一下头。|香味对了，掰开的声音不对。维伊说这是常见的顺序。}
# en: Add the warmth of the oven
opt.right.label [111260] = 加上烤炉的温度
# en: {Vey picks your loaf up and puts it down hastily, as if it had burnt her. The class actually applauds.|The bench beside you swears the room got warmer. It didn't. That's the point.|You add the warmth of the oven and the smell of the morning after. Vey takes your loaf home, she claims, by mistake.}
opt.right.say.1 [7b1411] = {维伊拿起你的面包，又匆忙放下，像被烫着了。全班真的鼓起了掌。|旁边那桌发誓屋里变暖了。并没有。这正是重点。|你添上了烤炉的温度和第二天清晨的气味。维伊把你的面包带回了家，她说是拿错了。}
# en: {The warmth arrives and the loaf leaves. You're left holding a hot, empty board.|Your bread steams, then smokes, then smells of a cupboard. Vey writes something short.|You add warmth, and the smell goes with it. The loaf is perfect and hot and smells of absolutely nothing.}
opt.right.say.2 [9771e5] = {温度来了，面包走了。你手里只剩一块发烫的空木板。|你的面包冒气，然后冒烟，然后有股橱柜味。维伊写下了很短的一句评语。|你添了温度，气味却跟着没了。面包完美、滚烫，而且一点味道都没有。}

@event illu_find_vey
# en: Find the Professor
title [4d9a54] = 找出教授
# en: {Professor Vey is rarely at the lectern in Illusion II. She is somewhere in the room, wearing someone else, and the first to name her wins.|Vey's chair is empty. Everyone eyes the porter with the mop.|The lectern is empty. You trust nothing in this room.} {There's a pigeon on the sill.|A student nobody remembers has taken the back row.|One of the portraits seems unusually attentive.}
text [93c884] = {幻术 II 的课上，维伊教授很少站在讲台后。她就在教室某处，扮成别人，第一个叫出她的人获胜。|维伊的椅子空着。大家都盯着那个拿拖把的杂役。|讲台空着。这间屋里你什么都不信了。} {窗台上有只鸽子。|后排坐着一个谁也不记得的学生。|有幅肖像画看起来格外专注。}
# en: A lecture hall where the professor's chair is empty and everyone is looking suspiciously at everyone else, including a pigeon on the sill.
scene [f6ad02] = 一间讲堂，教授的椅子空着，每个人都狐疑地打量着别人，包括窗台上的一只鸽子。
# en: Watch everyone, all lesson
opt.left.label [b92af8] = 整节课盯着每个人
# en: {You don't find her, but you notice who blinks late. Vey turns out to have been the pigeon.|At the end she steps out of the porter's coat. You'd suspected the mop. The mop was real.|You learn three classmates' nervous habits and nothing about Vey, who was the attentive portrait all along.}
opt.left.say.1 [e45672] = {你没找到她，但留意到了谁眨眼慢半拍。原来维伊是那只鸽子。|最后她从门房的外套里走了出来。你本来怀疑的是拖把。拖把是真的。|你摸清了三个同学的紧张小动作，却对维伊一无所知——她从头到尾都是那幅专注的肖像。}
# en: Name her early
opt.right.label [cf9752] = 抢先叫出她
# en: {You name her before the bell has finished ringing. She says, "Hm," which from Vey means a great deal.|"Professor," you say to the new student in the back row. The glamour falls away like a dropped shawl. Vey looks almost pleased.|You name the attentive portrait. The paint slides off Vey's face like a curtain. "Hm," she says.}
opt.right.say.1 [80bf8b] = {铃声还没响完，你就叫出了她。她说了声“嗯”，从维伊嘴里说出来，分量很重。|“教授。”你对后排那个新面孔说。魅影像一条滑落的披肩般褪去。维伊看上去几乎是满意的。|你叫出了那幅专注的肖像。颜料像帘子一样从维伊脸上滑落。“嗯，”她说。}
# en: {You accuse a perfectly ordinary classmate. He will remember it. So will Vey, who was standing behind you.|You accuse the quiet student in the back row, who turns out to be a quiet student in the back row. Vey was the mop.|You point at the portrait. The portrait points back. Vey, at the lectern after all, makes a note.}
opt.right.say.2 [4d12ea] = {你指认了一个再普通不过的同学。他会记住这件事。维伊也会——她就站在你身后。|你指认了后排那个安静的学生，结果那真的只是个后排的安静学生。维伊是那把拖把。|你指向那幅肖像。肖像也指向你。维伊原来就在讲台后，记了一笔。}

@event illu_courtyard_hour
# en: Holding the Courtyard
title [9a561c] = 撑住庭院
# en: {Advanced Illusion leaves the classroom. Hold an illusion over the busy courtyard for an hour, and don't let it fray.|Another courtyard hour. The porters step round you now.|The courtyard. {final_year: One of the last times you'll hold this sky.|Your hands know the weight of it.}} {A flock of swallows today.|Rain that doesn't wet anyone.|{season == "winter": Snow that never lands.|{season == "spring": Blossom that never lands.|{season == "autumn": Leaves that never land.|Thistledown that never lands.}}}}
text [3cbd95] = {高等幻术走出了教室。在热闹的庭院上空维持一个幻象一小时，别让它散开。|庭院一小时，照旧。杂役们现在会绕着你走。|庭院。{final_year: 这是你最后几次撑起这片天空了。|你的双手已熟悉它的分量。}} {今天是一群燕子。|淋不湿任何人的雨。|{season == "winter": 永远落不了地的雪。|{season == "spring": 永远落不了地的花瓣。|{season == "autumn": 永远落不了地的落叶。|永远落不了地的蓟花绒。}}}}
# en: A student standing very still in a busy courtyard, sweat on their brow, while a flock of illusory swallows circles above the crowd.
scene [84d039] = 一个学生一动不动地站在热闹的庭院里，额上冒汗，一群幻象燕子在人群上方盘旋。
# en: Hold it the full hour
opt.left.label [f25e9f] = 撑满一整个小时
# en: {By the end your head rings like a struck bell. Nobody looked up once, which is how you know it worked.|A first-year holds out a hand to catch something you made. You keep it falling for her until the bell.|You hold it, then sit on the fountain's edge for longer than you'd like anyone to see.}
opt.left.say.1 [40c796] = {结束时你的脑袋嗡嗡作响，像被敲过的钟。没有一个人抬头看过，这说明你成功了。|一个一年级生伸手去接你造出来的东西。你一直让它为她飘落，直到下课铃响。|你撑住了，然后在喷泉边坐了好一会儿，比你愿意让人看见的更久。}
# en: Keep it small and steady
opt.right.label [e4edc7] = 做小一点，求稳
# en: {You keep only a corner of it, perfect, for an hour. Vey says ambition is cheap and an hour is not.|You shrink it to a patch of weather over one bench. It never frays, and nobody notices, which is the point and the pity.|You keep it small: a few flakes over one bench, falling for the hour. A first-year sits under it and doesn't know why she's happy.}
opt.right.say.1 [2f1933] = {你只留住它的一角，完美无瑕，整整一小时。维伊说野心廉价，一小时可不廉价。|你把它缩成一张长椅上空的一小片天气。它始终没散，也没人注意到——这既是重点，也是遗憾。|你把它缩得很小：一张长椅上空飘着几片，落了整整一个钟头。一个一年级生坐在下面，不知道自己为什么高兴。}

@event illu_original_work
# en: An Illusion of Your Own
title [61c895] = 你自己的幻象
# en: {Original work, an illusion nobody taught you. Vey asks one question of each piece. "What does it make people feel?"|More original work. Vey's question hasn't changed; your answers get longer.|Studio morning. {final_year: Next year, Vey says, she'll ask someone else.|Vey goes round the room asking her question.}} {A classmate has made a door that sighs.|Someone has made the smell of rain on hot stone.|Someone's illusion is humming.}
text [2e4955] = {原创作业，一个没人教过你的幻象。维伊对每件作品只问一个问题。“它让人感受到什么？”|原创作业继续。维伊的问题没变，你的回答越来越长。|工作室的早晨。{final_year: 明年，维伊说，她就要问别人了。|维伊在屋里挨个问她的问题。}} {有个同学做了一扇会叹气的门。|有人做出了雨落在热石头上的气味。|有人的幻象在哼歌。}
# en: A darkened studio room, a student alone at the centre, and around them the half-formed image of a lit window at dusk.
scene [62326f] = 一间昏暗的工作室，一个学生独自站在中央，四周是一扇黄昏亮灯的窗户的半成形影像。
# en: Make something true
opt.left.label [dd57e1] = 做一件真实的东西
# en: {You make the window of a house you grew up near, at dusk. Vey stands in front of it a long time and writes nothing down.|You make a corridor that remembers who walked down it. It's sadder than you meant. Vey says that's usually the good sign.|You make the hum of a kitchen at night, kettle cooling. Vey sits down in front of it, which she never does.}
opt.left.say.1 [4d3103] = {你做出了童年附近一栋房子黄昏时的窗。维伊在它前面站了很久，什么也没写。|你做了一条记得谁走过的走廊。它比你预想的更悲伤。维伊说，这通常是好兆头。|你做出了夜里厨房的嗡嗡声，水壶慢慢凉下去。维伊在它前面坐了下来，她从不这样。}
# en: Make something dazzling
opt.right.label [9f8272] = 做一件耀眼的东西
# en: {A staircase of light climbs into the ceiling and keeps going. The class goes quiet. "Yes," says Vey. "But what does it feel like?"|Your piece fills the room with lanterns, one for each person watching. Vey counts them, and finds one for herself.|Your piece hums and blazes and then, at the end, goes very quiet and small. Vey writes "that last part" in her notes.}
opt.right.say.1 [664883] = {一道光之阶梯升进天花板，还在继续往上。全班安静下来。“是的，”维伊说，“可它感觉起来像什么？”|你的作品让满屋亮起灯笼，每个观看的人一盏。维伊数了数，发现有一盏是给她的。|你的作品嗡鸣、绽放，最后变得非常安静、非常小。维伊在笔记里写下“最后那一段”。}
# en: {It's dazzling for a breath and then empty, like a fair after the fair has gone.|Vey watches it all, politely. "Very bright," she says. You'd have preferred anything else.|It hums, and blazes, and Vey waits politely for it to stop. "And when it's over?" she asks. You don't have an answer.}
opt.right.say.2 [5c7316] = {它耀眼了一瞬，然后空了，像集市散场后的集市。|维伊礼貌地看完了全程。“很亮。”她说。你宁愿听到任何别的评语。|它嗡鸣、绽放，维伊礼貌地等它结束。“结束以后呢？”她问。你答不上来。}

@event beast_mucking_out
# en: Mucking Out
title [2efb0b] = 清理马厩
# en: {Beastcraft I begins in the stables, with a pitchfork. Professor Brask says you don't touch a creature until you've cleaned up after it.|Pitchforks. Brask still hasn't said when that rule ends.|The stables, early. You know which stall to start with.} {The hippogriff in the end stall is watching you.|Owls shift in the rafters, unimpressed.|{season == "summer": The heat doubles the smell.|A cold wind finds every gap.}}
text [99dfd0] = {驭兽学 I 从马厩和一把干草叉开始。布拉斯克教授说，没替一只生灵收拾过，就别碰它。|干草叉。布拉斯克仍然没说这条规矩什么时候结束。|清早的马厩。你知道该从哪个隔栏开始了。} {尽头隔栏里的鹰头马正盯着你。|猫头鹰在椽子上挪动，一脸不以为然。|{season == "summer": 热天让气味翻了一倍。|冷风钻进每一道缝。}}
# en: A student with a pitchfork in a straw-strewn stable, a hippogriff watching from its stall with a look of deep judgement.
scene [8f7a38] = 一个学生拿着干草叉站在铺满稻草的马厩里，一头鹰头马从隔栏里投来深深审视的目光。
# en: Muck out properly
opt.left.label [795f12] = 认真清理干净
# en: {Two stalls, a barrow and a blister. Brask inspects your work and calls the straw "nearly decent".|You finish before anyone else. The hippogriff treads straight through your clean straw, deliberately.|Brask says nothing, which you've learned is the best review she gives humans.}
opt.left.say.1 [390e61] = {两个隔栏、一辆推车、一个水泡。布拉斯克检查后说这稻草“勉强像样”。|你第一个干完。鹰头马故意从你刚铺好的干净稻草上踩了过去。|布拉斯克一言不发，你已经明白这是她给人类的最高评价。}
# en: Bow to the hippogriff first
opt.right.label [d249bf] = 先向鹰头马鞠躬
# en: {You bow low and hold it. The hippogriff considers, then bows back. Brask writes your name on the board, without comment.|The hippogriff lets you near enough to see where its feathers turn to fur. You'll remember the exact line.|You bow to the hippogriff in the end stall, as you always do now. It bows back before you've finished.}
opt.right.say.1 [d4557e] = {你深深鞠躬并保持住。鹰头马考虑了一下，回了一礼。布拉斯克在黑板上写下你的名字，不加评语。|鹰头马让你走近到能看清它的羽毛在哪儿变成皮毛。你会记住那条分界线。|你像现在每次那样，朝最里面隔间的鹰头马鞠躬。你还没鞠完，它就回礼了。}
# en: {You bow too fast. The hippogriff takes it as a challenge and accepts.|The hippogriff looks at your bow, then at your hat, and shoves you into the barrow to get at it. It eats the hat.|You bow and the hippogriff ignores you entirely, which is worse than the hat. You muck out under its scorn.}
opt.right.say.2 [03c9ed] = {你鞠躬太快了。鹰头马把它当成挑战，并且接受了。|鹰头马看了看你的鞠躬，又看了看你的帽子，一把把你拱进推车，够着了帽子。它吃掉了帽子。|你鞠了躬，鹰头马完全不理你，这比吃帽子还糟。你在它的鄙夷下清完了马厩。}

@event beast_hover_line
# en: The Hover Line
title [253240] = 悬停队列
# en: {Flight is half the course. Brask lines you up on the lawn to hover a foot up and hold still while she counts.|The hover line. Brask counts slowly on purpose, you're sure.|Hover line. You and your broom have an understanding, of sorts.} {Somebody's broom keeps edging toward the lake.|An owl has landed on the end of a broom, and its rider is pretending not to notice.|Brask says, as always, that brooms are harder to reason with than griffons.}
text [2eec93] = {飞行占这门课的一半。布拉斯克让你们在草坪上排成一行，离地一尺悬停，她数数时不许动。|悬停队列。你确信布拉斯克是故意数得这么慢。|悬停队列。你和你的扫帚已经算是达成了某种共识。} {有人的扫帚一直往湖那边挪。|一只猫头鹰落在一把扫帚的尾端，骑手假装没注意到。|布拉斯克照例说，扫帚比狮鹫难讲道理多了。}
# en: A line of students hovering a foot above a lawn on brooms, one broom drifting out of line, a stern professor counting slowly.
scene [10dd11] = 一排学生骑着扫帚悬停在离草坪一尺高的地方，一把扫帚偏离了队列，一位严厉的教授正慢慢数数。
# en: Hold still until the count
opt.left.label [37c0d2] = 一动不动直到数完
# en: {You hold it until forty. Your legs remember it for a day.|The broom bucks once at thirty-one. You hold on. Brask gets to fifty and nods.|Steady all the way. Brask says it's nice to see a broom that knows who's in charge, and she means the broom.}
opt.left.say.1 [749e71] = {你撑到了四十。你的腿记了一整天。|数到三十一时扫帚猛地一颠。你抓住了。布拉斯克数到五十，点了点头。|全程稳稳当当。布拉斯克说很高兴看见一把知道谁说了算的扫帚——她指的是扫帚。}
# en: Study how the others fall off
opt.right.label [4c91b6] = 研究别人怎么摔下来
# en: {You stand at the end and watch. You learn a great deal about balance, and nobody lets you forget you didn't fly.|You take notes on every wobble. Brask reads them and says you should consider a career in inquests.|You watch the owl on the broom-end win the hover line. Brask writes down the owl's name.}
opt.right.say.1 [ae91bb] = {你站在队尾观察。你学到了很多关于平衡的东西，也没人让你忘记你没飞。|你把每一次摇晃都记了下来。布拉斯克读完说你该考虑去当验尸官。|你看着那只落在扫帚尾上的猫头鹰赢下了悬停。布拉斯克记下了猫头鹰的名字。}

@event beast_feeding_round
# en: Feeding Round
title [d6808f] = 喂食巡回
# en: {Feeding round, in pairs. You and {partner} have two buckets and a list, and the griffon chick is first on it.|Feeding round with {partner}. The griffon chick has heard the buckets.|You and {partner} could do the round blindfolded now. The chick would still sulk.} {Brask has written "DO NOT HURRY" at the top of the list.|The owls lean down from the rafters to watch.|{partner} is humming to the buckets.}
text [34e935] = {两人一组喂食。你和{partner}有两只桶和一张清单，狮鹫雏鸟排在第一个。|和{partner}一起喂食。狮鹫雏鸟已经听见了桶的声音。|你和{partner}现在蒙着眼都能走完一圈。雏鸟照样会闹脾气。} {布拉斯克在清单顶上写着“不许着急”。|猫头鹰从椽子上探下身来看。|{partner}在对着桶哼歌。}
# en: Two students carrying buckets between stalls, a sulky griffon chick in a nest of straw, owls leaning down from the rafters.
scene [28f709] = 两个学生提着桶在隔栏间穿行，一只闹脾气的狮鹫雏鸟窝在草堆里，猫头鹰从椽子上探下身来。
# en: Take the griffon chick
opt.left.label [2348a0] = 负责狮鹫雏鸟
# en: {The chick eats from the bucket, then from your hand, then tries your sleeve. {partner} applauds quietly.|It sulks, then eats, then sulks about having eaten. Brask says that's progress for a griffon.|You and {partner} feed the chick in turns, humming. It sulks, but eats in rhythm.}
opt.left.say.1 [1639b7] = {雏鸟先从桶里吃，再从你手里吃，然后尝了尝你的袖子。{partner}轻轻鼓掌。|它闹脾气，然后吃，然后为自己吃了而闹脾气。布拉斯克说对狮鹫来说这就是进步。|你和{partner}轮流喂雏鸟，一边哼歌。它还在闹脾气，却跟着节拍吃完了。}
# en: {The chick bites the bucket, then the hand holding it. {partner} finishes the round alone, kindly.|It knocks the bucket over, and you with it, and sits in it, glaring. You spend the hour, bruised and soaked, fishing out its breakfast.|{partner}'s humming puts the chick in a mood. It takes the mood out on your hand.}
opt.left.say.2 [7f9047] = {雏鸟咬了桶，接着咬了提桶的手。{partner}好心地独自喂完了一圈。|它把桶打翻，连你也一起撞倒，然后坐在桶里怒目而视。你浑身淤青、湿透，花了一小时把它的早饭捞出来。|{partner}的哼歌惹得雏鸟心情不好。它把气全撒在了你的手上。}
# en: Take the owls instead
opt.right.label [40efde] = 改去喂猫头鹰
# en: {You learn the owls' names from the tags on their perches, and what a pellet is, in detail.|Up and down the ladder for an hour. {partner} survives the chick and is grateful in a quiet way.|The owls take their mice with great ceremony. One of them seems to be counting yours.}
opt.right.say.1 [436aaa] = {你从栖木上的名牌认全了猫头鹰的名字，还详细了解了什么是食丸。|在梯子上爬上爬下一小时。{partner}熬过了雏鸟那一关，默默地心怀感激。|猫头鹰们隆重地接过各自的老鼠。其中一只似乎在数你手里的。}

@event beast_hare_paddock
# en: Running with Hares
title [07bbef] = 与野兔同跑
# en: {Beastcraft II teaches haste the old way. Run with the hares until their speed rubs off. "Borrow it," Brask says. "Don't steal it."|The hare paddock. The hares remember you.|Hares. You dream in sudden right angles now.} {The grass is wet and the hares don't care.|Brask times you with a crooked hourglass.|{season == "summer": It's hot and the hares are lazy.|The paddock smells of rain.}}
text [54e3b7] = {驭兽学 II 用老办法教疾速：跟着野兔跑，直到它们的速度沾到你身上。“借，”布拉斯克说，“别偷。”|野兔围场。野兔们记得你。|野兔。你现在连做梦都是突然的直角转弯。} {草是湿的，野兔不在乎。|布拉斯克用一只歪斜的沙漏给你计时。|{season == "summer": 天很热，野兔很懒。|围场里有雨的气味。}}
# en: Students sprinting across a paddock alongside a scattering of brown hares, one student's feet suddenly much faster than the rest of them.
scene [853b14] = 学生们和一群棕色野兔一起冲过围场，其中一个学生的脚突然比身体其他部分快了许多。
# en: Run until it catches
opt.left.label [e48d98] = 跑到速度沾上身为止
# en: {For three strides you're faster than you've any right to be. Then you're in the hedge.|You catch it on the fourth lap, a lightness behind the knees. You pay for it with a nap you can't refuse.|The hares let you keep up for a moment, out of curiosity. It's the best moment of your week.}
opt.left.say.1 [5f6f03] = {有三步你快得毫无道理。然后你一头扎进了树篱。|第四圈时你抓住了它，膝盖后面一阵轻盈。代价是一场你拒绝不了的午睡。|野兔们出于好奇，让你跟上了一会儿。这是你这周最好的时刻。}
# en: Watch the hares and take notes
opt.right.label [5a946d] = 观察野兔，记笔记
# en: {You sketch the way a hare turns, everything at once, no warning. Brask says your sketch is better than your running.|You note how the hares rest between bursts. Brask reads it and says, "Yes. That's the half everyone forgets."|You sketch the hares in sudden right angles. Brask pins your page up by the paddock gate.}
opt.right.say.1 [42dee1] = {你画下野兔转身的样子，一切同时发生，毫无预兆。布拉斯克说你画得比跑得好。|你记下野兔在两次冲刺之间如何休息。布拉斯克读完说：“对。这是大家都忘掉的那一半。”|你画下野兔突然的直角转弯。布拉斯克把你那一页钉在了围场门边。}

@event beast_complaints
# en: The Complaints Hour
title [225734] = 投诉时间
# en: {Beast-speech practice. You sit on a bucket in the stables and listen. Every creature has been waiting to complain, and the owls start with the draught.|Another hour on the bucket. The owls open, as always, with the draught.|The bucket, the owls, the draught. Brask calls it fieldwork.} {The hippogriff wants different hay. It is very specific.|The griffon chick has a list.|{gpa >= 3: Brask leaves you alone with them, which feels like trust.|Brask stays near the door, which feels like supervision.}}
text [f1a417] = {兽语练习。你坐在马厩里一只倒扣的桶上倾听。每只生灵都早就等着要投诉，猫头鹰先说穿堂风。|还是那只桶，再坐一小时。猫头鹰照例先说穿堂风。|桶，猫头鹰，穿堂风。布拉斯克管这叫田野调查。} {鹰头马想换一种干草，要求非常具体。|狮鹫雏鸟列了一张清单。|{gpa >= 3: 布拉斯克让你单独和它们待着，像是一种信任。|布拉斯克一直守在门边，像是一种监督。}}
# en: A student sitting on an upturned bucket in a stable, surrounded by animals who all seem to be talking at once.
scene [1a419d] = 一个学生坐在马厩里一只倒扣的桶上，周围的动物似乎都在同时说话。
# en: Hear every complaint out
opt.left.label [770d17] = 把每条投诉听完
# en: {The owls talk for forty minutes about the draught. You understand every word now, which is the trouble.|The hippogriff explains its views on hay at length. You come away fluent and exhausted.|A mouse you didn't know was there wants to be on the record. You put it on the record.}
opt.left.say.1 [27f588] = {猫头鹰就穿堂风讲了四十分钟。你现在每个字都听得懂，麻烦就在这儿。|鹰头马详尽阐述了它对干草的看法。你出来时既流利又筋疲力尽。|一只你都不知道在场的老鼠要求记录在案。你把它记录在案了。}
# en: Fix the draught yourself
opt.right.label [79b85b] = 亲手把漏风堵上
# en: {You climb into the rafters with a hammer and a plank. The owls supervise. The draught stops, and so do the complaints, briefly.|You patch the gap with straw and a board. The owls say thank you, then mention the window.|You fix the draught. The owls thank you, then move on to the window, the hay and the mouse, in order.}
opt.right.say.1 [912b4b] = {你带着锤子和木板爬上椽子。猫头鹰在一旁监工。风停了，投诉也短暂地停了。|你用稻草和一块木板堵上了缝。猫头鹰道了谢，然后提起了窗户。|你修好了漏风处。猫头鹰道了谢，然后依次说起窗户、干草和那只老鼠。}

@event beast_lake_flight
# en: Over the Lake
title [abc6c7] = 掠过湖面
# en: {Advanced Beastcraft. A hippogriff each, over the lake, no saddle unless you ask. Brask won't think less of you for asking. She'll just remember.|The lake flight. Your hippogriff knows the way.|Over the lake. {final_year: You catch yourself memorising the view.|Your reflection keeps pace.}} {The water is perfectly still.|A barge below, its passengers waving.|{season == "summer": The air is full of midges.|The wind off the water stings.}}
text [2da61e] = {高等驭兽学。每人一头鹰头马，飞越湖面，除非你开口要，否则没有鞍。布拉斯克不会因为你要鞍而看轻你。她只会记住。|湖上飞行。你的鹰头马比你认路。|湖面上空。{final_year: 你发现自己在默默记住这片风景。|你的倒影一路跟着你。}} {湖水纹丝不动。|下方有一艘驳船，乘客们在挥手。|{season == "summer": 空中满是蠓虫。|湖面吹来的风刺痛脸颊。}}
# en: A student on a hippogriff's back skimming low over a mirror-still lake, their reflection racing along beneath them.
scene [20d2f8] = 一个学生骑在鹰头马背上低低掠过镜面般平静的湖，倒影在下方飞驰。
# en: Ride bareback, low over the water
opt.left.label [e0de3a] = 无鞍贴着水面飞
# en: {You skim so low a wingtip draws a line across the lake. For one breath you and your reflection touch hands.|The hippogriff banks and you go with it, as if you'd always known how. Brask says nothing at all, then grins.|You fly low enough for your reflection to keep pace, wingtip to wingtip. You don't want to land.}
opt.left.say.1 [5a8524] = {你飞得那么低，一侧翼尖在湖面划出一道线。有那么一口气的工夫，你和你的倒影碰了碰手。|鹰头马侧身转弯，你顺势而动，仿佛生来就会。布拉斯克一言不发，然后咧嘴笑了。|你飞得低到倒影能和你齐头并进，翼尖对着翼尖。你不想降落。}
# en: {The hippogriff dips and you don't. The lake is colder than it looks. It always is.|You slide off on the turn and hang on by a fistful of feathers, all the way back to shore.|You race your reflection and your reflection wins. You surface laughing, and very cold.}
opt.left.say.2 [d60787] = {鹰头马往下一沉，你没有跟上。湖水比看上去冷。向来如此。|你在转弯时滑了下去，攥着一把羽毛吊了一路，直到岸边。|你和自己的倒影赛跑，倒影赢了。你从水里冒出来，笑着，冷得要命。}
# en: Take the saddle and the high circuit
opt.right.label [6b0bf1] = 上鞍，走高处的航线
# en: {Saddled, high and steady. You see all seven towers at once, and nobody sees you.|The safe circuit, twice. Brask remembers, as promised, and nods at you all the same.|You take the saddle and the high circuit, and look down at the lake as if memorising it. Brask lets you take a second lap.}
opt.right.say.1 [92de41] = {上鞍，高飞，平稳。你一眼看尽七塔，却没人看见你。|安全航线，飞了两圈。布拉斯克果然记住了，但还是朝你点了点头。|你上了鞍，走高线，低头看着湖，像要把它背下来。布拉斯克让你再飞一圈。}

@event beast_manticore_rounds
# en: Manticore Rounds
title [f18c88] = 蝎尾狮巡检
# en: {Advanced students check the manticore once a month. Someone holds the tail; someone hums the lullaby. Brask lets you choose.|Manticore rounds. It knows the lullaby better than you do.|The manticore yawns at you, which is either a welcome or a threat.} {Its tail twitches in its sleep.|It has been off its food, Brask says, and is in a mood.|{final_year: You wonder who'll hold the tail after you.|Brask has brought a bucket of meat and a smaller one of patience.}}
text [c5506e] = {高年级学生每月检查一次蝎尾狮。一人握住尾巴，一人哼摇篮曲。布拉斯克让你自己选。|蝎尾狮巡检。那首摇篮曲它比你还熟。|蝎尾狮冲你打了个哈欠，不知是欢迎还是威胁。} {它的尾巴在睡梦中抽动。|布拉斯克说它最近不肯好好吃东西，正闹情绪。|{final_year: 你想知道你走后谁来握这条尾巴。|布拉斯克带来了一桶肉，和一小桶耐心。}}
# en: A manticore lying in straw with its eyes half-closed, one student gently holding its scorpion tail while another hums nearby.
scene [a03d57] = 一头蝎尾狮半眯着眼躺在稻草里，一个学生轻轻握着它的蝎尾，另一个在旁边哼歌。
# en: Hold the tail
opt.left.label [d27267] = 握住尾巴
# en: {You hold the tail still while Brask checks the sting. It's warm and heavy and does not, at any point, stab you.|The manticore lets you hold its tail the way a cat lets you hold a paw. Under protest, briefly, as a favour.|You hold the tail while Brask feeds it from the bucket. It eats from her hand and watches you the whole time.}
opt.left.say.1 [edb591] = {布拉斯克检查毒刺时，你稳稳握着尾巴。它温热、沉重，而且自始至终没有蜇你。|蝎尾狮让你握着它的尾巴，就像猫让你握它的爪子——不情不愿，片刻而已，算是赏脸。|布拉斯克从桶里喂它时，你握着尾巴。它从她手里吃，眼睛却一直盯着你。}
# en: {The tail flicks. You let go just in time, mostly. Sister Amaranth asks no questions; she's seen this course before.|It rolls over, tail and all, onto you. Nothing breaks, but you're bruised in the exact shape of a manticore.|It's in a mood, and the tail knows. You let go a moment too late and spend an hour with Sister Amaranth.}
opt.left.say.2 [d4a6ce] = {尾巴一甩。你及时松了手，大体上及时。阿玛兰斯修女什么也没问；这门课她见多了。|它连尾巴带身子翻了过来，压在你身上。没断什么，但你身上的淤青恰好是一头蝎尾狮的形状。|它心情不好，尾巴也知道。你松手晚了一刻，在阿玛兰斯修女那儿待了一个钟头。}
# en: Hum the lullaby
opt.right.label [978181] = 哼摇篮曲
# en: {You hum the whole lullaby twice, off-key on the high bit. The manticore sleeps through its own check-up.|You hum. A classmate holds the tail. Brask says the humming is the harder job, and nobody believes her.|You hum while Brask brings the meat. The manticore eats, slowly, and for once the mood lifts.}
opt.right.say.1 [58461b] = {你把整首摇篮曲哼了两遍，高音那段跑了调。蝎尾狮在自己的体检中一觉到底。|你哼歌，一个同学握尾巴。布拉斯克说哼歌才是更难的活儿，没人信她。|布拉斯克拿来肉时你在哼歌。蝎尾狮慢慢吃着，难得心情好了起来。}

@event umbral_dim_lamps
# en: Reading by Shadow
title [1839c4] = 借影识物
# en: {Umbral Theory I, top of the tower, lamps low on purpose. Name what's under each cloth by its shadow alone.|The cloths are back. The lamps are as low as ever.|Shadow reading. The dark no longer seems strange, which the professor says is the first lesson.} {One shadow is slightly larger than its object.|The professor moves the lamp an inch, and every answer changes.|{season == "summer": It's warm outside, never up here.|Rain on the windows makes the shadows shiver.}}
text [bfc068] = {暗影理论 I，塔顶，灯故意调得很暗。只凭影子说出每块布下面是什么。|布又盖回桌上了。灯和往常一样暗。|读影。黑暗不再显得陌生——教授说，这就是第一课。} {有一道影子比它的物体略大一点。|教授把灯挪了一寸，每个答案都变了。|{season == "summer": 外面很暖，这上面从来不暖。|窗上的雨让影子瑟瑟发抖。}}
# en: A dim lecture room at the top of a tower, objects hidden under cloths on a table, their shadows thrown long on the wall behind.
scene [3e8e65] = 塔顶一间昏暗的教室，桌上的物件盖着布，它们的影子长长地投在身后的墙上。
# en: Read them patiently
opt.left.label [21c0ff] = 耐心地读影子
# en: {A teapot, a skull, a folded letter addressed to you. You open it later. It's blank.|You name every shadow but one. Under that cloth there is nothing at all. The professor doesn't explain.|Slowly, you get them all. The shadows told you, the professor says; you only had to stop interrupting.}
opt.left.say.1 [962f6c] = {一把茶壶，一个头骨，一封写给你的折起来的信。你后来拆开，是空白的。|你认出了所有影子，只有一个例外。那块布下面什么也没有。教授没有解释。|慢慢地，你全认出来了。是影子告诉你的，教授说；你只是不再打断它们。}
# en: Slip in a false shadow
opt.right.label [131d22] = 混进一道假影子
# en: {You add the shadow of a cat to the wall. Three classmates write "cat". The professor writes your name, and underlines it.|Your false shadow passes all morning. The professor only catches it when it doesn't move with the lamp.|Your false shadow shivers with the rain like the real ones. Nobody finds it. The professor shakes your hand, which is cold.}
opt.right.say.1 [8fc52d] = {你在墙上添了一道猫的影子。三个同学写下“猫”。教授写下你的名字，还划了线。|你的假影子撑过了整个上午。直到它没跟着灯动，教授才发现。|你的假影子像真影子一样随雨发抖。没人发现它。教授和你握了手，那只手是冷的。}
# en: {Your false shadow points the wrong way. The professor turns it round gently, like straightening a picture.|Your shadow-cat sits up and leaves. It wasn't meant to do that. The professor doesn't seem surprised.|The rain makes every shadow shiver except yours. The professor notices the one that keeps still.}
opt.right.say.2 [b417db] = {你的假影子朝向反了。教授轻轻把它转了回来，像扶正一幅画。|你的影子猫坐起来，走了。它本不该这样。教授似乎并不意外。|雨让每道影子都在发抖，唯独你的没有。教授注意到了那道不动的影子。}

@event umbral_chalk_ward
# en: Pale Shells
title [003c50] = 苍白的壳
# en: {Ward drill, in pairs. One of you raises a pale shell over the other, and the professor lets the lamp-shadows loose along the floor to find the gap.|Pairs again. The professor's shadows have learned new tricks since last time.|The paired drill. You know how the shadows like to come: low, and from behind.} {Your partner's shell keeps flickering.|Your partner is a first-year who has never held a ward for more than a minute.|{gpa >= 3: The professor pairs you with the weakest student, on purpose.|The professor pairs you with someone as nervous as you are.}}
text [36de71] = {护界操练，两人一组。一人在另一人头上撑起一层苍白的壳，教授放出灯影沿着地面去找缝隙。|又是两人一组。教授的影子比上次多学了几招。|结对操练。你知道影子喜欢怎么来：贴着地，从背后。} {你搭档的壳一直在闪。|你的搭档是个一年级生，从没撑过一分钟以上的护界。|{gpa >= 3: 教授故意把你和最弱的学生分在一组。|教授把你和一个跟你一样紧张的人分在一组。}}
# en: Students behind faint, pale bubbles of light as a professor flicks pieces of chalk at them from the front of a dim room.
scene [710e30] = 学生们躲在一层层淡淡的苍白光罩后面，一位教授在昏暗的教室前方朝他们弹粉笔。
# en: Hold the shell over both of you
opt.left.label [bd8e9e] = 把护界撑在你们俩头上
# en: {You stretch your shell over your partner as well. The shadows nose along its edge for an hour and find nothing. You feel every touch in your teeth.|Two people under one ward is twice the weight. Yours holds until the bell, just.|The shadows give up on your shell and go after the next pair. The professor nods at you, once.}
opt.left.say.1 [6dfac8] = {你把壳也撑到搭档头上。影子沿着边缘嗅探了一整个钟头，什么也没找到。每一下触碰你都震在牙根里。|一个护界罩两个人，就是双倍的分量。你的撑到了下课，勉强。|影子放弃了你的壳，转去找下一组。教授朝你点了一下头。}
# en: Coach your partner through theirs
opt.right.label [a6ede4] = 指导搭档撑起自己的
# en: {You talk your partner through it, breath by breath. Their shell holds for nine minutes, then a shadow slips under it and makes you both jump. "Teaching," says the professor, "is also a ward."|You keep your own shell down and watch for the gaps in theirs. By the end, they've stopped flickering. You've learned where shadows like to get in.|You coach your nervous partner, and you're nervous too. The shadows come low and from behind; you both turn in time.}
opt.right.say.1 [d45323] = {你一口气一口气地带着搭档撑。他们的壳撑了九分钟，然后一道影子从底下钻了进来，把你们俩都吓了一跳。“教人，”教授说，“也是一种护界。”|你撤下自己的壳，盯着对方壳上的缝隙。到最后，他们的壳不再闪了。你也弄明白了影子喜欢从哪儿钻进来。|你带着紧张的搭档，自己也紧张。影子从低处、从背后来；你们俩都及时转过了身。}

@event umbral_quiet_minutes
# en: The Quiet Minutes
title [089065] = 静默的十分钟
# en: {Each lesson opens with ten minutes of silence. "Listen to what's hidden," the professor says, and puts out every lamp but one.|The quiet minutes. You can hear the tower settle, stone by stone.|Ten minutes of silence. You look forward to it, and also not.} {Someone's stomach rumbles at the worst moment.|The candle leans toward the door, though nothing comes in.|{season == "summer": A bee is lost in the room somewhere.|The wind hums in the stairwell.}}
text [540b0c] = {每节课都以十分钟的静默开始。“去听隐藏之物。”教授说，然后熄灭了所有灯，只留一盏。|静默的十分钟。你能听见塔一块石头一块石头地沉降。|十分钟的静默。你有点期待它，又有点不。} {有人的肚子在最不合适的时候叫了。|烛火朝门口倾斜，尽管什么也没进来。|{season == "summer": 屋里不知哪儿有只迷路的蜜蜂。|风在楼梯井里低鸣。}}
# en: A circle of students sitting perfectly still in near darkness, a single candle in the middle, everyone listening very hard.
scene [5f3b47] = 一圈学生在近乎全黑中一动不动地坐着，中间只有一支蜡烛，每个人都在用力倾听。
# en: Listen properly
opt.left.label [e31a7f] = 认真倾听
# en: {You hear the tower breathing, which it shouldn't, and a sigh on the stair that nobody makes.|You hear the lake, which is impossible from up here. The professor says that's normal for this room. It is not reassuring.|In the silence you hear someone you miss, very faintly. When the lamps come up, you don't mention it.}
opt.left.say.1 [0ee9e7] = {你听见塔在呼吸——它不该呼吸——还有楼梯上一声没人发出的叹息。|你听见了湖，从这里本不可能听见。教授说这在这间屋里很正常。这话并不让人安心。|静默里，你隐约听见一个你思念的人。灯亮起来时，你没提这件事。}
# en: Quietly finish other homework
opt.right.label [29deb1] = 悄悄写别的作业
# en: {You finish a whole essay by feel in the dark. The professor never notices, or never says.|Not a scratch of the quill. When the lamps come up, your essay is done and your face is innocent.|You write in the dark with the wind humming the rhythm. The essay is done when the lamps come up.}
opt.right.say.1 [c2c5c4] = {你在黑暗里摸索着写完了一整篇论文。教授始终没发现，或者始终没说。|羽毛笔一点声音都没出。灯亮时，你的论文写完了，脸上一派无辜。|你在黑暗里写着，风在楼梯间哼着节拍。灯亮时，论文写完了。}
# en: {When the lamps come up the professor is behind you, reading your essay. "Your third paragraph is weak," she says.|Your quill squeaks. In that silence it sounds like a scream. Everyone turns.|A gust slams the stairwell door and you drop your quill. It rolls, loudly, to the professor's feet.}
opt.right.say.2 [f43498] = {灯亮时，教授就站在你身后读你的论文。“你的第三段很弱。”她说。|你的羽毛笔吱了一声。在那片寂静里，听起来像一声尖叫。所有人都转过头来。|一阵风把楼梯间的门撞上了，你的羽毛笔掉了。它骨碌碌地、响亮地滚到了教授脚边。}

@event umbral_short_distances
# en: Short Distances
title [35c701] = 短距离
# en: {Umbral Theory II brings the shadowstep, desk to desk. "The shadows in between are not friendly," the professor says, "so don't linger."|Shadowstep drill. Three desks this time, then four.|The desks. You know the way between them, and the cold that lives there.} {Someone comes out under the wrong desk.|The lamps are lower than usual.|{gpa >= 3: The professor sets you the long way round.|The professor sets you the short way, and watches.}}
text [142afe] = {暗影理论 II 教影步，从一张桌子到另一张。“中间那些影子可不友善，”教授说，“所以别逗留。”|影步操练。这次三张桌子，然后四张。|这些桌子。你认得它们之间的路，也认得住在那里的寒意。} {有人从错误的桌子底下钻了出来。|灯比平时更暗。|{gpa >= 3: 教授让你绕远路。|教授让你走近路，并且盯着。}}
# en: A student stepping into the shadow under one desk and halfway out of the shadow under another, the room's lamps burning low.
scene [18d81b] = 一个学生踏进一张桌子下的影子，半个身子从另一张桌子下的影子里出来，屋里的灯低低燃着。
# en: Step across
opt.left.label [894fac] = 一步跨过去
# en: {In, through, out. It takes no time and lasts forever. You come out under the far desk with frost on your sleeves.|Four desks, clean. Something in between brushes your ankle, curious, and lets you pass.|You take your set route and come out exactly where the professor pointed. The cold in between nods at you, almost.}
opt.left.say.1 [83def2] = {进去，穿过，出来。不花一点时间，又像过了一辈子。你从最远那张桌子下出来，袖子上结了霜。|四张桌子，干净利落。中间有什么东西好奇地擦过你的脚踝，然后放你过去了。|你走指定的路线，正好从教授指的地方出来。中间的寒冷几乎朝你点了点头。}
# en: {You come out one desk short and somewhat upside down. The cold stays in your fingers until lunch.|You linger, just for a moment. It's enough. You come back pale, and the professor sits you by the one warm lamp.|The professor's route is longer than you'd like. You come out at the end, but so does the cold, with you.}
opt.left.say.2 [a8397a] = {你差一张桌子就出来了，而且有点头朝下。寒意在你指尖一直留到午饭。|你逗留了，只有一瞬。这就够了。你脸色苍白地回来，教授让你坐到唯一一盏暖灯旁。|教授给的路线比你想的长。你出来了，寒冷也跟着你一起出来了。}
# en: Map the route on paper first
opt.right.label [f66070] = 先在纸上画好路线
# en: {You draw every shadow in the room, and where it goes at each hour. The professor keeps your map.|You work out the route in ink and walk it once, slowly, in the light. It's dull, and correct.|You map the set route desk by desk. The professor checks your map and adds one shadow you'd missed.}
opt.right.say.1 [95dc62] = {你画下屋里每一道影子，以及它每个钟点会移到哪里。教授留下了你的图。|你用墨水推好路线，然后在光亮里慢慢走了一遍。枯燥，但正确。|你把指定路线一张桌子一张桌子地画了出来。教授检查后添上了一道你漏掉的影子。}

@event umbral_hidden_object
# en: Present but Unseen
title [a63725] = 在场而不可见
# en: {Hide a small key in this room, present but unseen. "Hiding is not removal," the professor says. "Removal is for amateurs."|The key, and somewhere to hide it. Your classmates are better at finding things.|The key exercise. Half the class pats their pockets out of habit.} {The key is brass today.|The key is silver and very cold.|Last time a key hid in a shadow for two days.}
text [c74599] = {把一把小钥匙藏在这间屋里，让它在场却不可见。“藏不是拿走，”教授说，“拿走是外行干的。”|钥匙，和一个藏它的地方。同学们找东西的本事见长。|钥匙练习。半个班都养成了拍口袋的习惯。} {今天的钥匙是黄铜的。|钥匙是银的，冰凉刺骨。|上次有把钥匙在影子里躲了两天。}
# en: A dim classroom being searched by several students at once while one of them sits calmly at a desk with a small brass key in plain sight.
scene [e384e8] = 一间昏暗的教室里，好几个学生同时在翻找，其中一个却平静地坐在桌旁，一把小铜钥匙就摆在眼前。
# en: Hide it, and stay calm
opt.left.label [7d28db] = 藏好它，保持镇定
# en: {You leave the key on the desk in plain sight, in your own shadow. Nobody sees it. The professor smiles, which is rarer than a key.|You hide it in the dark behind your own ear. They search the room twice and never once look at you.|You hide the key in a shadow and leave it there for two days, like the last one. Nobody finds it. The professor does, and approves.}
opt.left.say.1 [50e23d] = {你把钥匙明晃晃地放在桌上，就在你自己的影子里。没人看见。教授笑了，这比钥匙还难找。|你把它藏在自己耳后的暗处。他们把屋子搜了两遍，一次也没看你。|你像上一把那样，把钥匙藏进一道影子，放了两天。没人找到。教授找到了，表示赞许。}
# en: {A first-rate hiding place, found in under a minute by someone who simply asked the shadow.|You hide it so well you can't find it yourself. The professor retrieves it from the wall with a sigh.|You hide it in a shadow, and the shadow moves with the afternoon. By the bell the key is in the corridor.}
opt.left.say.2 [178ee3] = {一个一流的藏处，被人不到一分钟就找到了——对方只是问了问影子。|你藏得太好，连自己都找不到了。教授叹了口气，从墙里把它取了出来。|你把它藏进一道影子，可影子随着午后的光移动了。下课铃响时，钥匙已经到了走廊上。}
# en: Search for everyone else's
opt.right.label [69b186] = 去找别人藏的
# en: {You find four keys, one in a hat, one in a hinge, one in a shadow that didn't want to let go.|You find one key and a pencil nobody has missed for years. The professor counts both.|You find the key that hid for two days. It's still in its shadow, and you have to ask it nicely to come out.}
opt.right.say.1 [6d225e] = {你找到了四把钥匙：一把在帽子里，一把在合页里，一把在一道不肯松手的影子里。|你找到了一把钥匙，和一支多年没人想起的铅笔。教授两样都算数。|你找到了那把藏了两天的钥匙。它还在那道影子里，你得好言相劝它才肯出来。}

@event umbral_stair_wards
# en: The Old Stair Wards
title [a4469b] = 古老的阶梯护界
# en: {Advanced students renew the small wards on the tower's old stair. Some are newer than the stone. Some, the professor says, are much older.|The stair wards. You know which step hums.|The stair. {final_year: Someone else will kneel here next year.|Your knees know every step.}} {One ward is warm, as if someone's just left.|Something beyond a ward leans back when you touch it.|The stair lamps are mostly a suggestion.}
text [594d21] = {高年级学生负责加固塔里古老阶梯上的小护界。有些比石头新。有些，教授说，要古老得多。|阶梯护界。你知道哪一级会嗡鸣。|阶梯。{final_year: 明年会是别人跪在这里。|你的膝盖认得每一级台阶。}} {有一道护界是温的，像刚有人离开。|你一碰，护界另一侧有什么东西往后靠了靠。|阶梯上的灯基本只是个意思。}
# en: A student kneeling on an ancient spiral stair, hands pressed to a faint ring of light set into the stone.
scene [c60e93] = 一个学生跪在古老的螺旋阶梯上，双手按着嵌进石头里的一圈微光。
# en: Renew them carefully
opt.left.label [405067] = 仔细地加固
# en: {Step by step, ring by ring. Each ward takes a little of you and hums.|You renew eleven and pause at the twelfth. Leave that one, the professor says, and doesn't say whose it is.|At the top you're light-headed and the wards are bright. Something on the other side has gone quiet.}
opt.left.say.1 [84a4db] = {一级一级，一圈一圈。每道护界都取走你一点东西，然后嗡嗡作响。|你加固了十一道，在第十二道前停了下来。教授说那道别碰，却没说是谁的。|到了顶上你头晕目眩，护界都亮了。另一侧的什么已经安静下来。}
# en: Study the oldest ward instead
opt.right.label [6da660] = 转而研究最老的那道
# en: {You trace the oldest ring with one finger. The pattern folds in on itself like a knot nobody was meant to untie, and you feel watched for noticing even that.|The old ward is cold, careful work, made by someone who was afraid. You can feel the fear still in the stone.|You study the oldest ward by your hands alone, the lamps being no help. It's older than the stair. You're sure of that much.}
opt.right.say.1 [d84215] = {你用一根手指描着最古老的那一圈。那图案向内层层折叠，像一个本就不该被人解开的结；仅仅察觉到这一点，你就觉得被什么盯上了。|那道古老的护界是冰冷而小心的手艺，出自一个害怕的人。那份恐惧至今还留在石头里。|灯帮不上忙，你只凭双手研究那道最古老的护界。它比楼梯还老。这一点你很确定。}

@event umbral_errand
# en: The Shadow's Errand
title [febd12] = 影子的差事
# en: {Original work. Send your own shadow on an errand across the room, the professor says, and have it come back. "It will want to wander. They all do."|Shadow errands. Yours picks its own route now.|Errand day. {final_year: Does your shadow know you're leaving soon?|Your shadow seems eager, which worries you.}} {Someone's shadow is still under a desk from last week.|The professor's own shadow is missing today.|The lamps are low and the shadows long.}
text [e2911a] = {原创作业。派你自己的影子到屋子另一头办件差事，教授说，然后让它回来。“它会想乱跑。它们都这样。”|影子差事。你的影子现在会自己挑路线了。|差事日。{final_year: 你的影子知道你快要离开了吗？|你的影子显得跃跃欲试，这让你担心。}} {有人的影子从上周起还待在一张桌子底下。|教授自己的影子今天不见了。|灯很暗，影子很长。}
# en: A student standing in lamplight with no shadow at all, while across the room their shadow lifts a book from a shelf.
scene [fe154c] = 一个学生站在灯光下，身上没有一丝影子，而屋子另一头，他的影子正从书架上取下一本书。
# en: Send it, and trust it
opt.left.label [80242c] = 派它去，信任它
# en: {Your shadow crosses the room, lifts a book, and brings it back open at a page you needed. You didn't ask it to.|It comes back with a feather from the rafters, which wasn't the errand. The professor counts it as initiative.|Your shadow goes out long and comes back short, carrying a stub of candle. You don't know where it got it.}
opt.left.say.1 [f2385c] = {你的影子穿过屋子，取下一本书，带回来时正翻在你需要的那一页。你并没有叫它这么做。|它带回一根椽子上的羽毛，这不是差事内容。教授把它算作主动性。|你的影子拖得长长地出去，短短地回来，还带着一截蜡烛头。你不知道它是从哪儿弄来的。}
# en: {It comes back an hour late and a little the wrong shape. For a day it lags behind you on stairs, sulking, and you can't get warm.|It doesn't come back until dusk. When it does, it smells of the lake. The professor makes you sit with the lamp until your hands stop shaking with cold.|It stretches out under the low lamps and doesn't want to come back. When it does, it's longer than you for a day.}
opt.left.say.2 [9d55ca] = {它晚了一小时才回来，形状还有点不对。接下来一整天，它在楼梯上总落在你后面，闹着别扭，而你怎么也暖和不起来。|它直到黄昏才回来。回来时带着一股湖水的气味。教授让你在灯旁坐着，直到你的手不再冷得发抖。|在低矮的灯光下它伸得长长的，不想回来。回来后，一整天它都比你还长。}
# en: Keep it on a short leash
opt.right.label [bfc9a2] = 把它拴短一点
# en: {Your shadow goes as far as the window and no further. It looks out a long time before it comes back.|Two yards and home. Dull, safe and precise. The professor says precision is how shadow-workers get old.|You keep it close under the low lamps. It strains toward the long shadows and comes back to you, reluctantly.}
opt.right.say.1 [306102] = {你的影子走到窗边就停下了。它朝外望了很久，才回来。|两码远就回家。枯燥、安全、精确。教授说，精确就是影术师能活到老的原因。|在低矮的灯光下，你把它拴得很近。它朝那些长影子使劲，最后还是不情不愿地回到了你身边。}
